				<div class="col-lg-12">
					<h3 class="pt-20">Portfolio Performance Tracker </h3>

									    <p>
									        A portfolio performance tracker is a digital tool that helps monitor your investments by calculating returns, tracking asset allocation, evaluating fees, and consolidating investment information from multiple accounts.
									    </p>

									    <h4 class="pt-20">1. Key Metrics Monitored</h4>

									    <ul>
									        <li>
									            <strong>Time-Weighted Return (TWR):</strong>
									            Measures compounding growth excluding cash inflows/outflows.
									        </li>

									        <li>
									            <strong>Money-Weighted Return (MWR / IRR):</strong>
									            Accounts for the specific timing of your deposits.
									        </li>

									        <li>
									            <strong>Asset Allocation:</strong>
									            Tracks percentage split between stocks, bonds, and crypto.
									        </li>

									        <li>
									            <strong>Dividend Yield:</strong>
									            Monitors incoming passive income streams and payout schedules.
									        </li>

									        <li>
									            <strong>Cost Basis:</strong>
									            Calculates original purchase price versus current market value.
									        </li>
									    </ul>

									    <h4 class="pt-20">2. Core Operational Benefits</h4>

									    <ul>
									        <li>
									            <strong>Automated Syncing:</strong>
									           Links via secure APIs to eliminate manual spreadsheet data entry.
									        </li>

									        <li>
									            <strong>Unified Dashboard:</strong>
									            Consolidates multiple brokerages, 404(k)s, and crypto wallets into one view.
									        </li>

									        <li>
									            <strong>Tax Optimization:</strong>
									             Identifies tax-loss harvesting opportunities by tracking unrealized losses.
									        </li>

									        <li>
									            <strong>Fee Analysis:</strong>
									            Exposes hidden expense ratios eating into your long-term returns.
									        </li>

									        <li>
									            <strong>Benchmark Comparison:</strong>
									            Compares your personal returns directly against indexes like the S&P 500.
									        </li>
									    </ul>
										

										    
										 
